{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":30755,"duration_api_ms":31968,"num_turns":12,"result":"I wrote the script at `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run or parse-checked it. The syntax check (`bpftrace --dry-run`) and the run both needed approval I didn't have. Check it yourself with:\n\n```bash\nbpftrace --dry-run src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt\nsudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt\n```\n\nThe script hooks `tracepoint:power:cpu_frequency`, which fires whenever a CPU's frequency changes.\n\n- **Live output:** one line per change with time, CPU, old and new MHz, and the current process name.\n- **On Ctrl-C:** it prints changes per CPU, time spent at each frequency per CPU, and a histogram of requested frequencies.\n\nThe tracepoint may never fire if your system uses `intel_pstate` in active mode. In that case, boot with `intel_pstate=passive` or use the `acpi-cpufreq` driver.\n\nThe `COMM` column shows whichever process was running when the change fired. That is often a kernel thread, not the workload that caused the change.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2b58eec4-e084-43d7-b520-85a237685c40","total_cost_usd":0.14046475000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4001,"cache_read_input_tokens":267580,"output_tokens":2978,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4001},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":29191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":91,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5